    "engineLifespan": "300,000 - 450,000+ km. Hand-built by a single master technician at the AMG facility in Affalterbach (Germany), the M113 5.4L is a legendary naturally aspirated performance engine. Its lifespan is directly proportional to how rigorously it is maintained, as the extreme heat and performance limits tolerate zero neglect.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. Relying entirely on a massive 5.4-liter displacement, high-lift camshafts, and a high-flow intake to generate an instantaneous, brutal wave of 510 Nm of torque.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME 2.8 with bespoke AMG mapping. Features vastly sharper throttle response, raised rev limiters, and aggressive transmission shift protocols.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 3",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The rotating assembly utilizes a forged steel crankshaft, forged connecting rods, and specially coated forged aluminum pistons. The block is incredibly strong, easily handling aftermarket supercharger kits if desired.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "20.0 - 24.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "14.0 - 16.0 L/100km",
      "mixed": "16.5 - 18.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "26.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-40 or 0W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.3 or MB 229.5). The AMG engine runs significantly hotter than the standard V8s and requires premium, highly shear-stable synthetic oil to protect the forged internals.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Crankshaft Position Sensor (CPS) Failure: Like all M113 engines, the heat bakes the CPS, causing the car to suddenly stall when hot. The AMG engine runs even hotter, accelerating this failure.",
      "Valve Cover Gasket Oil Leaks: The extreme heat generated by the 5.4L engine quickly hardens the rubber valve cover gaskets. Oil leaks directly onto the massive AMG exhaust manifolds, creating a heavy burning smell and a potential fire hazard.",
      "Harmonic Balancer Rubber Separation: A well-known catastrophic flaw. The rubber isolation ring tears, allowing the outer pulley to wobble and machine a hole straight through the timing cover.",
      "Mass Air Flow (MAF) Sensor Contamination: The AMG engine requires immense airflow. Any contamination on the Bosch MAF sensor drastically reduces power and throws the engine into a rich-running condition.",
      "Ignition Coil and Spark Plug Wire Degradation: Sitting directly on top of the blistering hot magnesium valve covers, the 8 dual-output ignition coil packs and 16 high-tension wires bake and eventually crack, causing severe misfires under heavy load.",
      "Oil Filter Housing Gasket Leak: The gasket sealing the oil filter housing to the front of the block fails, leading to a massive oil leak that coats the alternator and serpentine belt."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Transfer Case Failure: The ML 55 AMG pushes a violent 510 Nm of torque through a BorgWarner transfer case originally designed for much weaker engines. Hard launches will stretch and eventually snap the internal drive chain, resulting in a total loss of drive.",
      "Astronomical Brake Replacement Costs: The ML 55 features massive, AMG-specific 4-piston Brembo front calipers and gigantic rotors (often referred to as the 'Porsche brakes'). When it is time to replace the pads and rotors, the parts cost is exponentially higher than a standard ML.",
      "722.6 Transmission 13-Pin Connector Oil Wicking: ATF leaks past the electrical pilot bushing O-rings and wicks up the wiring harness via capillary action, flooding and destroying the AMG-tuned Transmission Control Unit (TCU).",
      "Power Steering Pump Failure: The heavy AMG steering tuning, combined with high RPM cornering and massive tires, severely overworks the power steering pump, causing it to whine and eventually fail.",
      "Engine and Transmission Mount Destruction: The sheer rotational violence of the 5.4L V8 rips the fluid-filled rubber engine mounts apart rapidly. Once torn, the engine rests on the subframe, ruining the ride quality.",
      "AAM (All Activity Module) Electrical Failures: Early (2000-2001) ML 55 models suffer from the infamous pre-facelift body control module failures, leading to completely erratic lighting, locking, and starting issues."
    ],
