    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. Being a 2010-2011 engine, it is immune to the infamous early M272 balance shaft defect. The timing system here is highly robust.",
    "injectionType": "Bosch ME 9.7 Multi-point manifold port injection, uniquely mapped to operate on the Atkinson thermodynamic cycle to maximize thermal efficiency at the cost of low-end ICE torque (which the electric motors compensate for).",
    "engineLifespan": "The internal combustion M272 engine easily lasts 250,000+ Miles. HOWEVER, the hybrid high-voltage components, NiMH battery, and proprietary Two-Mode transmission are effectively end-of-life and unsupported. When the hybrid system fails, the vehicle is economically totaled.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated ICE paired with two high-output permanent-magnet synchronous electric motors integrated into the transmission housing.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME 9.7 paired with a vastly complex, proprietary Hybrid Powertrain Control Module jointly developed with GM, Chrysler, and BMW (The 'Two-Mode Hybrid' consortium).",
