    "oilSpecification": "8.5 Quarts 0W-40 or 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5). The engine experiences frequent auto-start/stop cycles, making premium lubrication absolutely critical.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "NiMH High-Voltage Battery Degradation: The 288-volt Nickel-Metal Hydride battery pack located under the cargo floor has aged out. Replacement packs are astonishingly expensive (often $10,000+) and incredibly difficult to source.",
      "Power Electronics Coolant Pump Failure: The dedicated electric water pump that cools the hybrid inverter and electric motors fails frequently. When it dies, the inverter overheats and completely immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "Two-Mode Transmission Glitches: The complex transmission, housing two electric motors and three planetary gearsets, is prone to electronic control failures and jerky engagements between electric and gas modes.",
      "Intake Manifold Tumble Flap Failure: Like all M272 engines, the plastic intake runner arms snap, throwing P2004-P2008 codes. This requires manifold replacement or a billet repair kit.",
      "Brake-by-Wire Regenerative Braking Faults: The transition between electric regenerative braking and mechanical hydraulic braking is managed electronically. Sensors fail, leading to inconsistent, grabby, or spongy brake pedal feel.",
      "Oil Cooler Seal Leaks: The rubber seals beneath the oil cooler in the engine's V-valley harden, causing oil to leak down the rear of the block."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Zero Dealership or Aftermarket Support: Because this vehicle was only sold in the US for two years in extremely low numbers, almost no Mercedes technicians know how to fix the hybrid system. Diagnostics are a nightmare.",
      "Economically Totaled by Hybrid Failure: If the bespoke hybrid inverter, transmission electric motors, or main battery pack fails, the cost of parts and specialized labor will vastly exceed the current market value of the entire vehicle.",
      "Front Differential Bearing Wear: The front differential is integrated into the complex hybrid transmission. When the bearings wear out (howling noise), repairing it without disturbing the electric motors is incredibly difficult.",
      "AIRMATIC Air Suspension Failure: The added weight of the hybrid battery pack puts extra strain on the rear air struts, which develop leaks and burn out the compressor.",
      "Command NTG Infotainment Glitches: The optical MOST ring network fails due to water ingress in the trunk, killing the audio and navigation system."
    ],
