    "author": ".",
    "riskRating": 4,
    "drivingExperience": "The W166 ML 350 represents a massive step forward in refinement over the previous generation. The naturally aspirated M276 V6 delivers 306 hp with an incredibly linear, silky-smooth power band. It completely lacks the agricultural harshness or vibration of the older M272. The integration of the 7G-Tronic Plus transmission is seamless, offering almost imperceptible gear changes. The chassis itself feels vastly superior to the W164—stiffer, quieter, and far more luxurious. While it won't win any drag races, it provides a profoundly comfortable, highly insulated, and effortless driving experience.",
    "mechanicVerdict": "The W166 ML 350 powered by the M276 engine is a watershed moment for Mercedes-Benz reliability. By completely redesigning the engine architecture to a 60-degree V-angle, Mercedes eliminated the need for a balance shaft—instantly eradicating the most catastrophic and financially ruinous failure point that plagued the older M272 V6. The core block and rotating assembly of the M276 are fundamentally bulletproof, easily capable of exceeding 400,000 km.\n\nHowever, this engine introduces BlueDIRECT technology (direct injection), which replaces old mechanical problems with new maintenance demands. Because fuel is injected directly into the combustion chamber, it no longer washes the intake valves. Carbon from the PCV system builds up rapidly; you must budget for a physical 'walnut blasting' of the intake valves around 100,000 km to restore idle quality and power. Furthermore, the Piezo injectors and High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) operate under immense stress and are highly sensitive to fuel quality; failures here are expensive.\n\nThe single most critical flaw you must look out for is the cold-start timing chain rattle. From the factory, oil drains out of the secondary chain tensioners overnight, causing the chain to slap violently for a few seconds on startup. If you buy this car, you MUST verify if the factory check valves (non-return valves) and updated tensioners have been installed. If ignored, the chain will stretch and destroy the cam phasers. Beyond the engine, the W166 chassis is very solid, though you must anticipate eventual AIRMATIC air strut replacements and be extremely wary of the rear bumper blind-spot radar sensors, which collect water, corrode, and can shut down the entire CAN bus network. Overall, if the chain tensioner fix is done, this is an exceptionally reliable and refined luxury SUV. 4/10 Risk Rating.",
    "repairCostEstimate": "800 - 1,400 EUR / year",
