        timingType: "Chain (Located at the front of the block. The M276 utilizes a complex primary and secondary chain system. Early iterations possess a catastrophic flaw: secondary tensioners lack non-return check valves. Oil drains out overnight, causing brutal chain slap on cold starts. If ignored, the loose chain violently stretches, skips teeth, and destroys the variable camshaft phasers. Installing updated tensioners and factory check valves is absolutely mandatory.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection (Bosch BlueDIRECT High-Pressure system at 200 Bar with piezoelectric injectors. This architecture prevents fuel from washing the intake valves. PCV oil vapor bakes onto the hot valve stems, creating severe carbon choking. Physical walnut blasting is required every 100k km. USA-spec is calibrated for AKI 91 and omits the European stratified lean-burn mode to meet SULEV emissions.)", 
