        vulnerabilities: [ 
            "Silitec Cylinder Bore Scoring - The absolute most catastrophic M157 flaw. The aluminum block uses a Silitec (Alusil) cylinder coating. Poor oil maintenance, extreme heat, or a stuck-open injector washes away the oil film, causing the piston skirts to deeply score the cylinder walls. This mandates a $20,000+ complete engine replacement.",
            "ECU Oil Inundation - If sacrificial pigtail harnesses are not installed on the cam sensors, oil wicks via capillary action directly into the Bosch ECU motherboard, completely destroying it and requiring a heavily coded AMG replacement.",
            "Bent Connecting Rods - While the internals are forged, tuner maps that request maximum boost (massive torque spikes) below 3,000 RPM will physically bend the connecting rods. Torque delivery must be mapped linearly.",
            "Timing Chain & Phaser Destruction - Ignored cold-start chain rattle lets the whipping chain stretch, skip teeth, and shatter the delicate AMG variable camshaft phasers, destroying the top end.",
            "Catastrophic Coolant Loss - If brittle plastic turbo coolant lines shatter completely while driving, the engine instantly dumps its coolant supply, leading to rapid warping of the handcrafted aluminum block.",
            "AMG 7G-Tronic Torque Converter Failure - Unlike the E63 AMG which uses an MCT wet clutch, the ML 63 retains the torque converter for towing/SUV duties. The 700 Nm of torque will shred the lockup clutch if the 60,000 km fluid interval is ignored."
        ],
