        timingType: "Chain (Located at the front of the block. The M278 V8 utilizes a highly complex timing system that is unfortunately notorious for premature tensioner failure. Extended oil change intervals or running incorrect oil viscosity causes the hydraulic tensioners to bleed down overnight, resulting in a loud metallic rattle on cold starts. Ignoring this rattle will inevitably lead to chain stretch, skipped timing, and catastrophic piston-to-valve contact.)", 
