            "Catastrophic Coolant Loss (Hot-V) - Brittle plastic turbo coolant lines inside the V-valley shatter completely while driving under boost, instantly dumping the ICE coolant supply.",
            "Lifter Collapse (Cylinder Deactivation) - Running low or dirty oil causes the specialized CAMTRONIC lifters to collapse, resulting in a severe misfire and requiring valvetrain surgery.",
            "Electric Water Pump Failure - The 48V electric water pump manages all ICE cooling. Sudden failure causes instantaneous block overheating.",
            "Engine-Out ISG Repair - Any mechanical failure or severe oil leak involving the Integrated Starter Generator requires complete removal of the transmission.",
            "AIRMATIC / E-ABC Total Collapse - The massive front-end V8 weight destroys the air struts. If equipped with E-Active Body Control, hydraulic pump failures are astronomically expensive."
